f(x)=0+0\\cdot x+o(x)$, but $f$ has no expansion $c_0+c_1x+c_2x^2+o(x^2)$.","$f(x)=x^2+o(x^2)$, since $f(x)=x^2$ for every $x>0$.","$f$ has no expansion even of first order, since $|x|$ is not differentiable at $0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dc33bc33f479353f908376d9","time_limit":40}]}}